# Implementation phases

> Purpose: **this is the list of what gets implemented.** Open this file to see what a phase includes and what is still open. Check the box when that deliverable is done. Current phase lives only in Profile (`P1`…`P5` | `done`). Never mix phases; finish the exit gate first.
>
> `phase-plan.mdc` does not replace this list. It only splits a P-item into functions (`U-nn`) for this project: file, inputs, tests. A deliverable is done when its box here is checked.

| Phase | Name | Focus |
|-------|------|--------|
| **P1** | Foundation | Concept lock, design + layout approved, tokens, skeleton, migrations (+ seeds) |
| **P2** | Mock UI + mock data | Every route built to `route-layouts.mdc` on mock adapters — no real API |
| **P3** | API backend | Real API on applied schema, endpoint by endpoint — UI stays on mocks |
| **P4** | Integration | Wire UI → API feature by feature; remove/replace mocks |
| **P5** | Cleanup & ship | Dead code, docs, regression, security/perf pass, deploy checklist |

## P1 — Foundation

**Goal:** everything later phases depend on is decided, written, and bootable — no feature UI yet.

- [ ] P1.1 **Intake complete** — Profile + `concept-domain.mdc` filled (entities, roles, statuses/lifecycles, business rules)
- [ ] P1.2 **Scope lock** — v1 in/out; feature list with IDs (`F-01…`) used by every later plan item
- [ ] P1.3 **Design direction approved** (AI proposal) → `frontend-design` skill + **Tailwind theme** tokens (colors, type, radius, shadow, spacing, z-index)
- [ ] P1.4 **Layout strategy chosen** + **`route-layouts.mdc`** filled and approved (every v1 route: mobile · tablet · desktop)
- [ ] P1.5 **Route & feature inventory** — route list × role, endpoint list (method, path, purpose), function inventory per feature
- [ ] P1.6 **`phase-plan.mdc` generated** — one or more `U-nn` rows for each P2–P5 item below; Function Specs on the critical path
- [ ] P1.7 **Repo skeleton** from `project-structure.mdc` for the Profile surface (`web` | `mobile` | `web + mobile`, one project) and flavor (`react` | `native`): `app/`, `api/`, `migrations/`, `seeds/`, `docs/`, `components/ui/`, `mocks/`, `tests/`, shared `types/contracts`
- [ ] P1.7a **Proposal package** (`proposal.mdc`) — **React** presentation only (not HTML), **Letter-size proposal document** (+ PDF), and guide skeleton in `docs/`; dev reviews → `APPROVED`
- [ ] P1.8 **Migrations** — one per entity, made with the Profile's migration tool (`db:new`): creates table/indexes/FKs, reversible when the tool supports it (`database.mdc`)
- [ ] P1.9 **Migration commands** — wrappers `db:new` · `db:up` · `db:down` · `db:status` · `db:seed` created and recorded in Profile → Migration tool; verified up → down → up (or fresh rebuild) on an empty DB
- [ ] P1.10 **Seeds** — via the tool's seeding mechanism, idempotent, demo data only from the concept (if needed), production-guarded
- [ ] P1.11 **`.env.example`** (keys only, incl. `APP_ENV`) + config loader `env()`; app boots empty; Profile → Environments + Deploy method recorded; live values only in **GitHub Environments/Secrets** (`environments.mdc`)
- [ ] P1.12 **UI scaffold** from `ui-components.mdc`: `components/ui/` groups + `lib/hooks/`, one stub per catalog component the concept needs (props + Component Spec header), plus the **component page** `/_components`; the `network/` group only if the concept has a networking/marketing plan
- [ ] P1.13a **Transition system** (`transitions.mdc`): motion tokens in the theme, `PageTransition`, `Presence`, `useNavDirection()`, `useReducedMotion()`; `useSwipeBack()` / `usePullToRefresh()` when Layout Responsive
- [ ] P1.13 **Layout shells scaffold** per strategy: `normal` → one `AppShell`; `layout` → `MobileShell`, `TabletShell`, `DesktopShell` + `ShellSwitcher`/`useViewClass()`; route folders (container + Mobile/Tablet/Desktop views) per `project-structure.mdc`
- [ ] P1.14 **Icon system** recorded (`material` | `fontawesome` | `flaticon` | `sf-symbols` | `lottie`; AI-recommended if the installer left it blank); 404/error/empty + skeleton + lazy-load plan noted
- [ ] P1.14a **Error console flags** (`error-log.mdc`): `.env.example` keys (`APP_DEBUG`, `VITE_DEBUG_PANEL`/equivalent, `APP_ENV`), template copied, `errorLog.init` behind the flag, production-stripped
- [ ] P1.15 **Tooling**: lint, format, test runner, hooks working (`/lint`, `/test`); `.github/workflows/ci.yml` from `templates/ci/` (PR checks); branches `develop` + `main`

**Exit (P1 → P2):** schema matches concept; migrate up/down/up passes; theme + shells + primitives stubbed; every v1 route has an approved layout block; `phase-plan.mdc` exists; proposal package approved (Letter PDF, no leftover `{{placeholders}}`); no feature UI pretending to be done. Then the **exit gate** below must pass. Do not start P2 before that.

## P2 — Mock UI + mock data

**Goal:** every v1 route works visually and behaviorally on **mocks**, built exactly to `route-layouts.mdc`. The default path is full enough to demo: no blank sections, no empty lists, no “lorem” standing in for real fields.

- [ ] P2.1 **Mock data — enough to show the product whole** — `mocks/<entity>.ts` fixtures + `mockApi.<entity>.list()/get()/create()/update()/remove()` matching the future real contract (same shapes, same error format); simulated latency + error toggles
  - Every screen’s happy path is populated: landing sections the route lists, lists, detail pages, dashboards, charts, admin records, and forms that display saved values
  - Enough rows to show the real layout (a list looks like a list, a chart has a series, a landing step has its copy and media). Not one stub row and not placeholder text
  - Names, dates, money, and statuses follow the concept. Copy reads like the real product (“Maria Santos booked a grooming visit”), never “demo here”, “demo dito”, “demo doon”, “lorem”, “test user”, or “sample item”
  - Do not copy another product’s content
  - Empty, loading, and error stay available as toggles. They are not the default demo
- [ ] P2.1a **Demo walk** — click through every v1 route on mocks at mobile, tablet, and desktop. Each section that should have content has content before P2 can exit
- [ ] P2.2 **Contracts/types** — request/response types per endpoint (single source reused in P3/P4)
- [ ] P2.3 **Components finished** — every catalog component the routes use is implemented, themed, keyboard + focus + a11y, with all states and its entry on the component page (light + dark, three widths)
- [ ] P2.4 **Form system** — every control in `forms.mdc`; `FormField` error slots; client validators as named functions (`validateEmail()`, `validateRequired()`, … or schema per form)
- [ ] P2.5 **Routing shells** — router, guards (`RequireAuth`, `RequireRole` on mock session), lazy-loaded route chunks, `PageTransition` wired with each route's `Transition:` from `route-layouts.mdc`
- [ ] P2.6 **Route-by-route build** — for each route in `route-layouts.mdc`, in plan order:
  - page component + its child components (each a `U-nn` under this item)
  - **mobile · tablet · desktop layout exactly as specified** (or reflow per `normal`), at the high-level direction in `frontend-design/SKILL.md` — not a plain junior layout
  - data hooks (`use<Entity>List()`, `use<Entity>()`, mutations) calling `mockApi`
  - all states: **skeleton** → loaded · **empty** · **error** (retry) · success feedback
  - tables: card list (mobile) · condensed table + drawer (tablet) · full table (desktop) where specified
- [ ] P2.7 **Forms wired** — submit handlers (`onSubmit`), disabled/loading state, inline field errors, no double-submit
- [ ] P2.8 **Shared screens** — animated **404**, status-error, empty data
- [ ] P2.9 **Navigation** — navbar/rail/sidebar/bottom tabs per class, back behavior, tab pages
- [ ] P2.10 **Layout & transition verification** — each route at 375 · 768 · 1280 against its block; transitions forward · back · deep link · refresh · rapid back-tap · reduced motion; fix drift
- [ ] P2.10a **Error console** — `<ErrorConsole/>` + `ErrorBoundary` mounted; `getContext` returns route ID + view class; mock errors (UI/API/status) verified in the popup
- [ ] P2.11 **Mock inventory** — list every mock module + consumer (for P4 removal)
- [ ] P2.12 **SEO stubs** only if Profile SEO = `on`
- [ ] P2.13 **Admin CMS** (when an admin or staff role exists) — CRUD screens (list, detail, create, edit, remove) for records and content, plus Letter print views, charts, and the year/month/day calendar picker per `admin.mdc`

**Exit (P2 → P3):** every route matches its layout block on all three classes; the demo walk shows each screen full on mocks (no blank happy path); no real API coupling; mock inventory written; ui primitives reused (no one-offs); 404/empty/skeleton/lazy present; contracts/types complete for P3. Then the **exit gate** below must pass. Do not start P3 before that.

## P3 — API backend

**Goal:** the real API, built **endpoint by endpoint**, matching the P2 contracts. UI still on mocks.

- [ ] P3.0 **Error envelope** — `requestId` on every request, `{ error, requestId, debug? }` (debug only when `APP_DEBUG=true` and not production), `GET /health`
- [ ] P3.1 **Bootstrap** — router, request/response helpers, `jsonSuccess()` / `jsonError()` (one consistent shape), error handler, CORS from env, request logging
- [ ] P3.2 **DB access** — `Database::query()`/`execute()` with **prepared statements only**; transaction helper
- [ ] P3.3 **Migrations applied** on local DB; seeds usable
- [ ] P3.4 **Auth** — `register()`, `login()`, `logout()`, `refresh()`/session, `me()`, password hashing/verify, token/session issue + expiry
- [ ] P3.5 **Middleware** — `authenticate()`, `requireRole(...roles)`, ownership check `canAccess(user, resource)`, rate limit on auth
- [ ] P3.6 **Validation layer** — server validators per endpoint as named functions; **every write validated server-side**; errors map to field names matching the UI form fields
- [ ] P3.7 **Endpoints, one by one** — for each endpoint, a Function Spec: route, handler, service, repository, validator, authz, response shape, error cases, tests. Typical set per entity: `list` (filter/sort/paginate), `get`, `create`, `update`, `delete` (soft-delete if norm), plus concept-specific actions. Admin CMS modules get this full set (`admin.mdc`)
- [ ] P3.8 **Special endpoints** if in concept: file upload (type/size/path checks), payments, notifications, exports
- [ ] P3.9 **Per-endpoint tests** — happy · validation fail (422 with field errors) · unauthenticated (401) · forbidden (403) · not found (404)
- [ ] P3.10 **API smoke run** — Postman-style/manual collection covering every endpoint; saved in repo
- [ ] P3.11 **Contract list** — final routes + payloads vs P2 contracts; diffs noted for P4

**Exit (P3 → P4):** every inventory endpoint done with tests; authz enforced server-side; prepared statements everywhere; contract diffs listed; UI still on mocks is OK. Then the **exit gate** below must pass. Do not start P4 before that.

## P4 — Integration (API ↔ UI) + mock cleanup

**Goal:** the UI runs on the real API, feature by feature, with no silent mock fallbacks.

- [ ] P4.1 **API client** — `apiClient.request()` (base URL from env, auth header, JSON, timeout), typed wrappers per endpoint; error normalization
- [ ] P4.2 **Auth wiring** — login/logout/refresh, session persistence, `RequireAuth`/`RequireRole` on real session, 401 → sign-out flow
- [ ] P4.3 **Feature-by-feature cutover** (not big-bang): for each feature in plan order — swap `mockApi.<entity>.*` for real service functions, verify, then delete that mock's usage
- [ ] P4.4 **Error mapping** — API field errors → form field errors; status codes → shared error/empty/404 screens
- [ ] P4.5 **Loading/empty/error** verified on real latency and real empty data
- [ ] P4.6 **Pagination / filters / infinite scroll** wired to real query params
- [ ] P4.7 **Mocks removed or quarantined** — only behind an explicit dev flag, never in production builds
- [ ] P4.8 **SEO meta + Schema.org** if SEO = `on`
- [ ] P4.9 **End-to-end happy paths** per role on the real API
- [ ] P4.10 **Layout re-check** — real data (long text, many rows) at 375 · 768 · 1280

**Exit (P4 → P5):** no silent mock fallbacks in prod builds; remaining mocks listed for P5 delete; integration bugs triaged; e2e paths pass. Then the **exit gate** below must pass. Do not start P5 before that.

## P5 — Cleanup, documentation, final testing

- [ ] P5.1 **Delete** dead code, unused routes/components, leftover mocks and flags
- [ ] P5.2 **Docs** — README/setup/env, migrate + seed commands, API reference (endpoint list), GitHub Secret **names** (not values)
- [ ] P5.3 **Regression pass** — roles × critical flows × three layout classes
- [ ] P5.4 **a11y** spot-check (forms, focus, contrast, reduced motion) and **security** smoke (authz, uploads, injection, secrets scan)
- [ ] P5.5 **Performance** sanity — main pages, bundle/lazy chunks, image sizes
- [ ] P5.6 **Deploy** — `/deploy setup` done (workflows from `templates/ci/`, GitHub Environments + secrets complete in each); staging deployed and verified with the `/deploy` checklist; production promoted with approval; rollback tested
- [ ] P5.6a **Production has no debug** — `APP_DEBUG=false`, no `debug` in responses, error-console code absent from the production build
- [ ] P5.7 **Phase notes closed**; `phase-plan.mdc` rows for finished P-items are `done`/`deferred`; Profile Current phase = `done`

**Exit (P5 → done):** no open P1–P4 items unless the dev marked them `deferred (reason)`. Ship only when the **exit gate** below passes.

